From 764bb4c1b99c76efdbc617d9d29c2b861f9eb58b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 10:43:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rtrafd/webui: v1.3.1 - fix Traffic Analyzer
 per-device/per-network (hardware offload bypassed conntrack); live probe;
 QoS-off class-panel messaging

Root cause (on-metal): with the Broadcom flow accelerator ON, LAN<->WAN traffic
is forwarded in hardware and never traverses the software path, so conntrack
byte counts and the br* bridge counters stay ~0. WAN (eth0 port counter) and
per-class (Runner queue counters) still see it, which is why only those worked;
per-device/per-network read the wrong source.

- rtrafd: replace the conntrack per-client collector with a flow-cache reader
  (/proc/fcache/nflist). Deltas each flow's cumulative TotalBytes per flow-id
  slot (recycle-safe), attributes uploads by the real LAN source IP/MAC, and
  correlates NAT'd download flows back to the client via the shared nf_conn[0]
  pointer. Per-network derived by mapping each client's LAN device to its
  bridge (/sys/class/net/<dev>/master, cached). This is offload-accurate.
- poll_ifaces: drop the br* branch (software-bridge counters miss offloaded
  flows); WAN still uses the authoritative eth0 counter; per-network now from
  the flow cache.
- Fallback: when nflist yields no flows (accelerator OFF - the software QoS
  engines Traditional/Cake do this), fall back to conntrack, which IS accurate
  on the software path. No double counting (offloaded flows' conntrack bytes
  freeze at offload; when accel is on nflist carries them and conntrack is
  skipped). Confirms Traffic Analyzer works across QoS off / HW QoS / SW QoS.
- Live probe: report the running average since the current 5-min bucket opened
  instead of the ring slot (only stamped at bucket close -> read 0 mid-window).
- www: per-class panel shows an explicit state ('enable HW QoS Classful' /
  'QoS is running <mode>, which has no per-class queues') when qos_type != 11,
  instead of a blank chart. FAQ accuracy note updated to flow-cache sourcing.
- rtrafd start/store logs raised to LOG_NOTICE so they appear in logread.

EXTENDNO=Reaper_v1.3.1. Syntax-checked + mock-validated (class gate renders,
ASCII clean). Metal test owed: Top devices + By network populate with real
per-client data under load with the accelerator ON (the fix's core claim),
across QoS off and a QoS mode; probe latency graphs; logread shows rtrafd.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
